
## PostgreSQL

`src/db.rs` serves `POST /notes` and `GET /notes/{id}` over an ordinary `sqlx::PgPool` built from `[database]` in `alloy.toml`. Outside local development, set `FERRUM_ALLOY_DATABASE_URL` (or `FERRUM_ALLOY_DATABASE_URL_FILE`) instead of committing credentials. The pool connects lazily: a database outage makes `/readyz` report not ready rather than stopping the service.

Migrations live in `migrations/` and are embedded at build time. They never run implicitly. Apply them as a separate step, once per release, before the new version serves traffic:

```bash
cargo run -- migrate
```

`database.migrate_on_startup = true` applies them at every start instead, from every replica; use it for local development only.

Queries are checked at runtime (`sqlx::query_as`), so building needs neither a database nor `.sqlx/` offline metadata. If you adopt the compile-time `sqlx::query!` macros, commit the `cargo sqlx prepare` output in `.sqlx/` so that CI never needs a database to build.

Tests that need a database are ignored by default:

```bash
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/postgres cargo test -- --include-ignored
```

The CI workflow runs them against a PostgreSQL service container.
